{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Chosen.</b> Selected. בָּחוּר is singular — every single chariot in this count was chosen." "<b>And all the chariots of Egypt.</b> And with them all the rest of the chariots. And from where were these animals? If you say from the Egyptians — behold it is stated ״וַיָּמָת כֹּל מִקְנֵה מִצְרָיִם״ (Exodus 9), and if from Israel — behold it is stated ״וְגַם מִקְנֵנוּ יֵלֵךְ עִמָּנוּ״ — whose were they? From those who feared the word of YHWH. From here would Rabbi Shimon say: the best of the Egyptians — kill; the best of the serpents — crush its brain (Mekhilta)." "<b>And third in rank over them all.</b> Officers of armies, as the Targum renders."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:05.003552422Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}